  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Sudan Peacebuilding Programme (SSPP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The South Sudan Peacebuilding Programme (SSPP) will be a central tool for delivering the UK&#x2019;s peace and stability objectives in South Sudan. The programme will:

1)	Build the capabilities of communities, including women, in conflict hotspots to manage, reduce, and prevent violent conflict in increasingly inclusive ways;
2)	Deploy technical experts to the peace agreement and ceasefire monitoring mechanisms to strengthen their capabilities to spur regional action to implement the peace agreement; and
3)	Produce bespoke, demand-driven conflict and political economy analysis to inform UK policy and programming in South Sudan, including by strengthening conflict sensitivity.</narrative>
  </description>
